{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3438","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3438","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3438\",\"parent_revision\":\"593a68ff6bc167ba0dd9e08c92b1d3cbd52070c73fdf0a4c5467fbb688dc9641\",\"root_revision\":\"593a68ff6bc167ba0dd9e08c92b1d3cbd52070c73fdf0a4c5467fbb688dc9641\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-06\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nTwo implementations now check whether a plugin's runtime files reference things that only resolve in this repo.\\n\\n- plugins/plugin-creator/skills/lint/scripts/audit_runtime_escapes.py, a reporting scanner with --plugin-dir and --all modes, which writes a markdown report.\\n- tests/test_plugin_self_containment.py, a pytest guard.\\n\\nThey were written independently and neither knows about the other. Their scan populations differ: the scanner covers skills/ and agents/ only, so it cannot see commands/, plugin-root CLAUDE.md, plugin-root references/, or docs/ \u2014 and real escapes live in those. The two therefore disagree about what counts as a finding.\\n\\nIMPACT\\n\\nOne rule with two enforcement points drifts. A fix that satisfies one can leave the other failing, and a rule change has to be made twice or the two silently diverge. This is the duplication the runtime-versus-design-time work exists to remove, reproduced inside that work.\\n\\nThe scanner also carries two defects of its own: the report header is hardcoded to \\\"development-harness runtime escapes\\\" regardless of which plugin was scanned, and it attributes the report to scripts/audit_dh_runtime_escapes.py, a path that no longer exists.\\n\\nACCEPTANCE\\n\\nRun both against plugins/agent-orchestration and against plugins/development-harness. List the lines each finds that the other does not, then decide which implementation absorbs the other rather than keeping both.\\n\\nUser-provided context: the scanner's exemptions were deliberate decisions, not accidents \u2014 fenced blocks are never findings so a document can show an anti-pattern verbatim, angle-bracket placeholders name a shape nothing resolves, and the repo-root directory list omits scripts and docs because both are valid inside a plugin. Whichever implementation survives needs to keep those, and the reasoning is recorded in plugins/plugin-creator/MAINTENANCE.md.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Post-rebase review, 2026-09-06\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"170dbcf1f09d0ecfa97d9cda57fb1afe8a82651676aa352c69d0906a61d47043\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABTSBZHQ\"}"}